In <4192@unido.informatik.uni-dortmund.de>, ks@Germany.EU.net writes:
> 
> To avoid frustrations during playing NH, I'm saving every new level I
> go down to be able to restart after a stupid death.

There is a special mode for what you are doing, called exploration mode.
You start with a wand of wishing with 3 charges, and whenever you die,
the program asks you whether you really want to die or not. You shouldn't
really be saving levels, since that is cheating :-) (exploration mode
won't put you on the score list when you are done). I haven't used it
for a while, but try the -X option.

